From: Animesh Kumar <animesh.kcm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qa_scoring: assert DIMENSION_WEIGHTS sum to 1.0 at import time

The rubric documented in README.md:206-213 relies on the QA dimension
weights summing to exactly 1.0. Future edits could break the invariant
silently. Add a single-line assertion that catches drift at import time.

Reported in improvements/code-review.md#cr-03.

---
 src/agents/qa_scoring.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/agents/qa_scoring.py b/src/agents/qa_scoring.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/agents/qa_scoring.py
+++ b/src/agents/qa_scoring.py
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ DIMENSION_WEIGHTS = {
     "compliance": 0.20,
     "communication_clarity": 0.15,
 }
+assert abs(sum(DIMENSION_WEIGHTS.values()) - 1.0) < 1e-9, (
+    "DIMENSION_WEIGHTS must sum to 1.0; check src/agents/qa_scoring.py "
+    f"(current sum: {sum(DIMENSION_WEIGHTS.values())})"
+)

 SYSTEM_PROMPT = (
     "You are an experienced call center quality coach. "
